        "Shakespeare shows power as ultimately self-defeating — Macbeth gains the throne and loses everything. Browning shows power as absolute and unchallenged — the Duke's 'I gave commands' is casual, chilling precisely because it is not dramatic. Both writers use form to expose their subject: Shakespeare through dramatic action; Browning through the dramatic monologue's ironic self-revelation.",
