        "Duffy's 'War Photographer' and Owen's 'Exposure' both explore the way war is experienced and consumed. Owen shows the soldiers' physical and psychological suffering; Duffy shows how that suffering is mediated, commodified and ultimately ignored by comfortable Western audiences. Together they argue that war's cost is both borne by soldiers and evaded by civilians.",
