        "In 'Ozymandias', power over the individual is ultimately futile — time defeats the tyrant. In 'London' (Blake), power oppresses the individual — 'mind-forged manacles' trap the urban poor in a system they cannot escape. The contrast is between power that collapses on its own and power that endures through the mind's internalisation of its own chains.",
